    content: "Cindy is a desktop app that runs AI coding agents (Claude Code and Codex) for you.\n\n**Your first session:**\n\n- Click **+ New** in the top of the left sidebar.\n- Choose the **agent** (Claude Code or Codex).\n- For code work, choose a **working directory** — the agent runs its file ops there. (You can skip this for plain-Q&A sessions.)\n- Optionally pick a **model** in the composer toolbar.\n- Type your goal and send.\n\n**Iterating:**\n\n- A session is a persistent chat thread: ask, review the result, then ask the next thing.\n- While the agent is replying, the **Send** button becomes **Stop** — click it to interrupt. You can keep typing in the meantime; follow-ups queue up and send in order.\n- Type `/` in the composer to open the slash-command palette (see the Commands topic).\n\n**Organizing:**\n\n- All sessions are listed in the left sidebar (see the Sidebar topic). Switch between them by clicking; each session remembers its agent, model, and working directory.\n- Keep unrelated tasks in **separate** sessions — sharing one session for everything dilutes context.\n\n**Tone tip:**\n\n- Describe the goal and context first, then what result you want. That works better than a single short command. The agents respond well to \"here's what I'm trying to do, here are the constraints, here's what 'done' looks like\".",
